      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant you interact with now runs on a newer version of its underlying model. It quietly swapped in a more recent release of the Sonnet model, so any conversation that relies on Sonnet automatically uses the updated one without you doing anything. You wouldn't see a button or setting for this; the only sign would be that responses may feel slightly sharper or more current. The change is already active, so if you chat with the assistant now, you're already benefiting from it.",
